export anchor IconRailMasterDetailStyle:
    number: 174
    screen: ProjectsDashboard
    name: Icon rail master-detail
    idea: A three-pane work surface where a slim dark icon rail, a white list pane with the greeting, figures and projects, and a wide detail pane for the selected project sit side by side, quiet slate with one blue.
    base: light
    palette:
        rail: #1e2733, the 64px icon rail
        railInk: #b8c4d2, rail icons that are not current
        railCurrent: #34425a, the current rail item behind a white icon and a white edge bar
        canvas: #f4f6f8, the detail pane background and the search field
        surface: #ffffff, the list pane, cards, the top bar and the style sheet
        ink: #1c2430, text
        muted: #5a6576, meta, labels, dates and day letters
        line: #dde2e8, every border and divider
        accent: #3451a8, the primary button, links, the selected row edge, meters, this week bars and focus
        selected: #eaf0fb, the selected project row
        lastWeek: #8794a8, outlines of last week bars
        ok: #1a7048, On track text and icon on a pale green chip
        risk: #8f5200, At risk text and icon on a pale amber chip
        bad: #b42318, Behind and overdue text and icon on a pale red chip
    type:
        One system stack, system-ui, Segoe UI, Roboto, Helvetica Neue,
        Arial. Base 14px at 1.45. The detail title is 26px at 650 weight,
        the greeting 20px, figures 20 to 22px with tabular numbers, card
        titles 15px, meta 12 to 13px, and pane labels 12px caps tracked
        0.06em.
    layout:
        Three columns at full height. A 64px dark slate rail holds a white
        square B mark, six icon-only links with tooltips and accessible
        names, Home current with a lighter tile and a white edge bar, and
        the initials disc at the foot. Next a 336px white list pane holds
        the greeting, the date and a pale red overdue line, then the four
        figures as a two by two ruled grid, then a Projects label and six
        full-width rows with name, status chip, category and due date, and a
        thin meter with percent and task counts. Mobile app 2.0 is selected
        with a pale blue fill and a blue left edge. The detail pane fills
        the rest. Its white top bar has search, New project, a bell and Mara
        Okafor. Below sit a breadcrumb, the project title with its At risk
        chip, meta with days left, an Edit project button, underlined tabs,
        a ruled four-cell facts strip, and then the team chart and the team
        activity side by side in bordered cards, activity for this project
        tagged. Below 1180px the cards stack. Below 760px the rail becomes a
        sticky top bar of icons and the panes stack.
    spacing: An 8px unit. 20px pane padding, 24px detail padding, 12px row padding, 20px between detail blocks.
    density: Medium to dense. Three panes visible at once, compact rows, small type.
    corners: Small. 6px panes and cards, 4px buttons, fields and chips, round initials.
    borders: 1px light slate lines between panes, rows and fact cells. The selected row has a 3px blue left edge.
    shadows: None. Separation comes from borders and the dark rail.
    icons:
        Line icons at 1.75px stroke, 22px in the rail, 18px elsewhere.
        Status uses a check circle for On track, a triangle with a bang for
        At risk, a crossed square for Behind and a clock for overdue, always
        with the word.
    focus: A 2px blue outline offset 2px, white on the dark rail.
    tone: Plain and neutral, such as Tasks completed, all projects and Team activity.
